 orchestrator error after us-east. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1.\n  - I ran the same rollback again, since rolling back to a known-healthy release is safe to repeat, and it finished in every region.\n- **Current state:** us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0. The error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to open it timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying. The incident had been created, so I didn't retry, which avoids paging on-call twice. Its summary covers the failed v2.3.1 deploy, the partial rollback, the second attempt and the current state.\n\nTwo things still need follow-up: finding out why v2.3.1 failed before anyone redeploys it, and the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}